senses.gloss:
तपस् + -धन + .({@-नः@}) ‘rich in penance’, an ascetic, devotee; रम्यास्तपोधनाना
 क्रियाः Ś. 1. 13; शमप्रधानेषु तपोधनेषु 2. 7, 4. 1; Śi. 1. 23;
 R. 14. 19; Ms. 11. 242.

तपस्य + .{@-स्यः@}
—1 The month of Phālguna; Bhāg. 12. 11. 40.
—2 An epithet of Arjuna.

तप्त + -कृच्छ्रम् a kind of penance consisting in drinking hot water, milk
 and ghee for three days each, and inhaling hot air for three days; Ms. 11. 214;
 Y. 3. 318.
